<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rato sees good August employment data.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rato sees good August employment data.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said August employment figures, due to be released in mid-September, will be positive.</p>
<p>&quot;(The figures will be) good, considerably better than in August of last year,&quot; Rato told a breakfast radio programme.</p>
<p>Spain's unemployment rate was 15.08 percent in August 1995 and 13.67 percent in July 1996.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2161</p>
